WEBVTT

00:00.490 --> 00:06.220
<b>So Koge-Donbo
used SD in her manga,</b>

00:06.330 --> 00:10.560
<b>and then Director Sakurai</b>

00:11.400 --> 00:16.030
<b>used it for the anime too.</b>

00:16.140 --> 00:21.800
<b>And that's why the anime series
has a very SD feel to it.</b>

00:24.410 --> 00:28.970
<b>Did Broccoli select the opening song?</b>

00:29.080 --> 00:30.780
<b>Who sings it?</b>

00:30.880 --> 00:39.630
<b>Note: King Records is the music label
and video distribution company that
released Di Gi Charat.</b>

00:30.880 --> 00:36.160
<b>No, this was determined by TBS.
Oh no, it's King Records.</b>

00:36.160 --> 00:37.730
<b>Yes, it was King Records.</b>

00:37.730 --> 00:39.630
<b>They made the recommendation.</b>

00:39.730 --> 00:43.900
<b>Note: This commentary was recorded
in August, 2004.</b>

00:39.730 --> 00:43.900
<b>But if you listen to it now,
you can tell how old this series is.</b>

00:43.900 --> 00:45.300
<b>It's talking about Y2K.
It's already 2004.</b>

00:45.300 --> 00:48.200
<b>It's talking about Y2K.
It's already 2004.</b>

00:51.110 --> 00:54.800
<b>This part with Rabi-en-Rose</b>

00:54.910 --> 00:58.900
<b>has been drawn
by Koge-Donbo many times.</b>

00:59.010 --> 01:01.500
<b>Yes, she hides behind the wall
and peeks out.</b>

01:01.620 --> 01:04.910
<b>Usada always comes out
from behind a wall.</b>

01:06.420 --> 01:09.790
<b>And they used it in the anime.</b>

01:10.620 --> 01:14.690
<b>This sign that says ''kuukan'' (space)
comes out often too.</b>

01:14.800 --> 01:17.630
<b>I wonder what it means.</b>

01:17.730 --> 01:19.200
<b>Kuukan Cafe?</b>

01:19.300 --> 01:21.960
<b>A cafe? Isn't it just space?</b>

01:22.070 --> 01:23.900
<b>So they're just promoting space?</b>

01:24.000 --> 01:26.840
<b>Yeah, and why does the sign
have an eye?</b>

01:26.940 --> 01:29.170
<b>I have no clue.</b>

01:30.680 --> 01:36.410
<b>We didn't know
what the anime would be like,</b>

01:36.520 --> 01:41.450
<b>and we only read
a lot of storyboards.</b>

01:41.560 --> 01:44.350
<b>We thought,
''Some of them have no ending.''</b>

01:44.830 --> 01:46.790
<b>But they said,
''That's what's great about it.''</b>

01:46.890 --> 01:48.520
<b>We didn't understand that.</b>

01:49.260 --> 01:52.960
<b>That's the feeling of
Di Gi Charat anime.</b>

01:54.070 --> 01:59.510
<b>And we would rudely tell the director,
''There's no ending!''</b>

01:59.610 --> 02:01.800
<b>But he'd say, ''This is perfect.''</b>

02:01.910 --> 02:04.170
<b>I also told him,
''I didn't get it.''</b>

02:04.280 --> 02:09.980
<b>So when the fans say
they don't get it,</b>

02:10.080 --> 02:13.950
<b>the same thing
happened to Broccoli too?</b>

02:14.050 --> 02:16.020
<b>Of course we thought that.</b>

02:16.120 --> 02:18.090
<b>And then we said,
''I guess it's okay.''</b>

02:18.190 --> 02:21.650
<b>But we didn't understand most of it.</b>

02:38.080 --> 02:42.520
<b>We also wondered</b>

02:44.550 --> 02:47.750
<b>how Usada's character
was going to be handled.</b>

02:47.860 --> 02:50.820
<b>Dejiko was already like this.</b>

02:52.330 --> 02:53.790
<b>Oh, there's Bukimi.</b>

02:54.030 --> 02:56.830
<b>Bukimi's already on screen.</b>

02:56.930 --> 03:02.430
<b>They are not an anime original, but
Koge-Donbo created them from the start.</b>

03:02.540 --> 03:08.200
<b>When I faxed the designs over
to MADHOUSE, they were surprised.</b>

03:08.310 --> 03:11.000
<b>''What the heck are these characters?''</b>

03:11.950 --> 03:16.380
<b>Are they modeled
after anyone in particular?</b>

03:16.950 --> 03:18.980
<b>Not really.</b>

03:19.490 --> 03:26.020
<b>They're like the typical otaku
in Japan.</b>

03:26.630 --> 03:31.090
<b>But they're probably
how Koge-Donbo see the otaku.</b>

03:32.300 --> 03:34.530
<b>I guess she's right, though.</b>

03:35.870 --> 03:38.770
<b>But the name ''Bukimi''
was created by the director.</b>

03:38.870 --> 03:42.470
<b>We didn't make it.
I think it's a wonderful name.</b>
